# Release Readiness Checks

Apply when validating **deploy / release readiness** or **production cutover** (broader than day-to-day commits).

**Overlap:** Same core commands as **`pre-commit-quality-gate`**; this rule adds deploy/auth/DB bootstrap sanity. Use pre-commit for every PR; use this before tagging, going live, or large infra/auth changes.

## Planning Mode

- In planning mode, do not run release validation commands.
- Capture release checks as deferred execution steps.
- Run this gate only after the user approves execution-mode implementation.

## Required Validation

- Run: `pnpm run lint`
- Run: `pnpm run tsc`
- Run: `pnpm run test`
- Run: `pnpm run build`

## Deployment/Auth Sanity

- Verify environment mapping docs are updated (`docs/configuration.md`, deployment docs).
- For auth changes, verify:
  - `/api/auth/login`
  - `/api/auth/me`
  - callback behavior and configured redirect URLs.

## Hosted DB Safety

- Use `db:migrate` + `db:seed` for hosted bootstrap.
- Do not use destructive local-import commands on hosted databases.

## Optional smoke

- After deploy, `DEPLOY_URL=... pnpm run smoke:deploy` when URLs/env are available (see `docs/development-workflow.md`).

## Feature flags / staged rollout

- If release touches **reader comfort**, **API base URL**, or other **VITE_*** toggles, cross-check `docs/development-workflow.md` (e.g. Reader Comfort Rollout) and `docs/configuration.md` so production env matches intent.

## Supply chain (advisory)

- Scheduled **`pnpm audit --audit-level high`** runs in `.github/workflows/audit-scheduled.yml`; review failures on a cadence, not only at release.
